    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear offensive anchor. With a commanding score of 81.26, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a rare alignment of a high-leverage leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Dobbins. The dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) positions him as our primary engine for stolen bases, a category we are aggressively targeting today. Flanking him at the top of the lineup, **Yordan Alvarez** (65.52) and **Junior Caminero** (62.27) remain locked in; while **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher SP_xERA in Woo, his elite 0.465 xwOBA justifies his status as a \"Strong\" play regardless of the matchup, while **Junior Caminero** leverages his #3 spot to mitigate a slightly tougher park environment. **Kyle Schwarber** also warrants attention at 60.40, as his leadoff role against Kremer maximizes his opportunities to anchor our HR and R totals.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Caleb Durbin** on the bench. Despite a solid score of 48.55, he failed to crack the starting nine because his profile relies heavily on stolen bases against a pitcher who, despite a slow delivery, holds a competitive 3.56 xERA. We opted for the higher floor offered by **Colt Keith** (50.92) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (52.89), both of whom benefit from favorable lineup placement and projected run production. Our primary concern remains **Gary Sanchez** (41.24), who is tethered to a \"Marginal\" start today; facing an elite arm like Skubal (2.77 xERA) suppresses his ceiling significantly, but he remains in the lineup due to the lack of a superior alternative. We are monitoring the situation closely to ensure we don't bleed too many game caps on an outing that could easily descend toward a floor-level performance.",
